--TEST--
A child placed `on: "worker"` and given `limits:` is held to that sub-cap on the core it was placed on: the narrowing crosses with the child rather than keeping it home — `rule:security/isolate-budget-is-the-trees`, `rule:concurrency/on-worker-runs-the-child-on-another-core`
--FILE nvs.toml--
# `rule:security/capability-check-at-the-door`: `spawn script` goes through a
# door that asks for `script.spawn` first, and a case with no configuration
# cannot spawn at all.
[capabilities.script]
spawn = true

# The tree's own ceiling, wide enough that what stops the child below is the
# sub-cap alone and not this number — `rule:security/isolate-budget-is-the-trees`.
[limits]
memory = "256M"
--FILE--
<?nvs
// The method form is the one that crosses a core: its label is looked up in the
// compiled unit's class table, which every core already holds, where a path
// would need a resolver the far core was never installed with
// (`crates/nvs-host/src/placed.rs`'s `# Known gaps`).
final class Greedy
{
    // `uint` because that is what `Core\Arr::count` answers, and a declared
    // `int` would be a narrowing conversion this language does not make silently.
    public static function fill(int $rows): uint {
        array<int> $held = [];
        for (var $i = 0; $i < $rows; $i = $i + 1) {
            $held[] = $i;
        }
        return Core\Arr::count($held);
    }
}

// Well past the `limits:` this child was placed under and well inside the tree's
// own. A limit breach is `rule:errors/on-limit`'s `FATAL`, which no `catch` in
// the child would see — it arrives here as `ok = false` instead.
var $capped = spawn script Greedy::fill(...)
    with(args: ["rows" => 400000], limits: {memory: "1M"}, output: "capture", on: "worker");
var $stopped = await $capped;
echo "capped ok=", $stopped->ok ? "true" : "false", "\n";

// The same entry and the same placement with nothing written beside it: the
// negative control, without which the line above would read the same on a worker
// core that could not run this at all.
var $wide = spawn script Greedy::fill(...)
    with(args: ["rows" => 400000], output: "capture", on: "worker");
var $done = await $wide;
echo "uncapped ok=", $done->ok ? "true" : "false", "\n";
echo "uncapped held ", $done->value as string, "\n";
--EXPECT--
capped ok=false
uncapped ok=true
uncapped held 400000
